<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov green coffee imports up 36 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov green coffee imports up 36 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports in November totalled 26,411 tonnes, up 36 percent from the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Thursday.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee amounted to 386 tonnes in November against 207 tonnes the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of green coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Nov 96	   Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p> Total	   26,411	   33,428	   19,417</p>
<p> Indonesia	5,949	    7,989	    4,376</p>
<p> Colombia	 4,462	    6,927	    4,137</p>
<p> Brazil	   8,618	    7,350	    5,129</p>
<p> Guatemala	  844		652		345</p>
<p> Honduras	   155		564		152</p>
<p>Cumulative green coffee imports in the first 11 months of 1996 were 302,482 tonnes, against 238,118 tonnes in the same period of the previous year.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Nov 96	  Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p>			 386	     484		207</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +813 3432 7431</p>
